{
  "_about": "Azulejo design tokens. Single source for colours (per theme), radii, spacing, type, status icons, symbol sizes and motion. The macOS shell reads them through apps/macos/Sources/Azulejo/Design.swift, generated by scripts/design-tokens; the core reads the themes too (azulejo-config, for user themes and the terminal palette), and so will the Linux shell (M3). atom-one-dark's colours come from docs/design/mockup-v1.png (One Dark). Hex colours are #rrggbb or #rrggbbaa. Keys starting with an underscore are notes. docs/themes.md describes the themes and the user theme format.",
  "version": 2,
  "defaultTheme": "atom-one-dark",
  "colorTokens": {
    "_note": "The colour tokens every theme defines, with what each is for. Theme colours live under themes.<id>.color. A value is \"#rrggbb\" / \"#rrggbbaa\", or {\"system\": NSColor name, \"alpha\": optional 0-1 replacing the colour's own alpha, \"hex\": the colour as macOS draws it by default in that theme's appearance}; the macOS shell resolves system colours live (they follow the user's accent colour), other platforms, webviews and tests use hex.",
    "window": "window background, gutters between tiles, toolbar row",
    "sidebar": "sidebar card, tab bar, tile header strip",
    "tile": "tile body: terminal backdrop, browser, preview, files",
    "tileAlt": "secondary tile bodies",
    "sunken": "browser chrome, code blocks, inset strips",
    "control": "segmented tracks, search field, tab container",
    "selected": "selected sidebar row, selected palette row",
    "selectedStrong": "strong selection grey: preview borders and table rules",
    "border": "hairlines around cards, fields and toasts",
